Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::the_direct_memory_access_wait_returns_once_its_deadline_has_passed`.

The defect: the IDMAC wait restarts its deadline on any change in the owned descriptors, not only
on one closing, so a controller that sets a descriptor's `OWN` bit again keeps the wait open for
as long as it likes.

Expected to fail: `the driver read the clock again after its deadline had passed`, in the
adversarial clock.
diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/internal_direct_memory_access.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/internal_direct_memory_access.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/internal_direct_memory_access.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/internal_direct_memory_access.rs
@@ -439,7 +439,7 @@
                 return Ok(());
             }
             let now = self.registers.now_microseconds();
-            if now_owned < owned {
+            if now_owned != owned {
                 owned = now_owned;
                 start = now;
             } else if now.wrapping_sub(start) > DATA_DEADLINE_MICROSECONDS {
